{"id": "DfZBSBTzLCQ", "title": "Video by feartalkies", "description": "A drum beat through the city: every wife, hide from the king. One wife climbed onto her roof… and let him see her. 🥁\n\nLast tale's answer: Vikram said the husband. One can understand the wife and her lover dying, they were desperately in love. But Manivarman saw his wife dead for another man, a moment that calls for anger, and he was so far from angry that, in his great love, he died of grief.\n\nVikram & Betaal: The Woman on the Roof.\n\nThe parts we couldn't fit in the reel: the king refused his own citizens too, when they gathered and begged him to take her. And the book's own line about the general: the actions of devoted followers are inexplicable. (The funeral pyre in the reel is our retelling of the book's \"he entered the fire\".)\n\n(From Somadeva's Ocean of Story, the Vetala tales.)\n\nSo, who was more loyal? The general who gave everything… or the king who said no? 👇\n\n#vikrambetaal #indianhorror #ghoststories #indianfolklore #horrorstories", "channel": "feartalkies", "uploader_id": "58803293522", "uploader": "Fear Talkies | Indian Horror", "timestamp": 1793948455, "like_count": 626, "comment_count": 9, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1146538491123185a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 67.257, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQOKUMzyq86VFx2VgfoTmRdVuA4S9P6X9wwD1KdQQeskg4tVh8_1Irj4mdxmwjacqrlAN50KtPX5VFYvdyrm7W4yVD-0nGtXxzdamqE.mp4?_nc_cat=110&_nc_oc=AdrfPBe3xcGrFkl7fuBUi0ccTqNP3IqarbynSAKdxWLguQIAQHLiHvb6GT3zrtnGg_lyTC1yxSK3jicVqU6